.SH NAME
file2sm \- shared\-memory linked list data ingestion test program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBfile2sm\fR \fIfileName\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBfile2sm\fR stress-tests shared-memory linked list data ingestion by repeatedly
writing all text lines of the file named \fIfileName\fR to a shared-memory linked
list that is the root object of a PSM partition named "file2sm".
.PP
After writing each line to the linked list, \fBfile2sm\fR gives a semaphore to
indicate that the list is now non-empty.  This is mainly for the benefit of
the complementary test program \fBsm2file\fR\|(1).
.PP
The operation of \fBfile2sm\fR is cyclical.  After copying all text lines of
the source file to the linked list, \fBfile2sm\fR appends an EOF line to
the linked list, containing the text "*** End of the file ***", and prints a
brief performance report:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&        Processing I<lineCount> lines per second.
.Ve
.PP
Then it reopens the source file and starts appending the file's text lines
to the linked list again.
